    "narrative": "For today\u2019s Independence Day slate, **Lawrence Butler** and **Tyler Freeman** anchor the lineup with the highest efficiency scores of the day at 74.61 and 72.83, respectively. **Lawrence Butler** benefits from a premium spot in the #3 hole and a favorable matchup against Alcantara, where his platoon advantage provides a +13% boost to his already solid base projection. **Tyler Freeman** is bolstered by a potent combination of a hitter-friendly park and a weak opposing arm in Ray (4.76 xERA). Meanwhile, **Luis Arraez** earns a start in the MI slot due to a high-ceiling matchup against the vulnerable Sullivan; his +19% SP skill boost makes him a core play to stabilize our AVG category despite the slight platoon friction.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was leaving **Taylor Ward** sidelined. Despite a respectable 41.87 efficiency score, he was squeezed out by the sheer volume of high-scoring options across our OF and UTIL spots, particularly with **Jung Hoo Lee** seeing a massive boost from the same favorable Sullivan matchup that elevates **Luis Arraez**. Elsewhere, we are closely monitoring the 40% rain risk surrounding **Bryson Stott**. While his 64.54 score makes him a lock to start, the weather could impact his ability to generate opportunities for us in the SB category, which remains our primary concern in this 5x5 format.\n\nWe continue to navigate a depleted roster with **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Will Smith**, and **Matt Chapman** remaining on the IL, placing heavy pressure on **Cal Raleigh** to provide power from the C1 spot. **Cal Raleigh** sits at a 64.17 efficiency, and while he faces a tough arm in Bieber, his placement in the #4 order slot keeps him as a must-start. We will continue to evaluate the potential for promotion from our farm system\u2014including **Dylan Beavers**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Ryan Waldschmidt**, and **Drew Gilbert**\u2014if our bench efficiency continues to struggle to crack the 50-point threshold in the coming weeks.",
